description:
FOUND s494u (Opus, 2026-09-28) attributing its companion re/ movers: at 209e7533 (main at s494u's launch; identical on the s494u tree, A/B'd) t/re/regexp_noamp.t regexp_normal.t regexp_notrie.t regexp_qr.t regexp_qr_embed.t regexp_trielist.t regex_sets_compat.t are all DIFF 0/0 with `aborted-forms:2: Modification of a read-only value attempted at (eval N) line N.` -- the snapshot (baselines/perl-suite-run.tsv) still carries e.g. regexp_normal.t 2021/8, regex_sets_compat.t 1755/274, regexp_noamp.t 796/109 TIMEOUT: a large PRE-EXISTING loss the snapshot has not seen yet (NOT spliced by s494u -- not its cause).  Each of those files is `for $file ('./re/regexp.t', ...) { if (-r $file) { do $file or die $@; exit } }`, and re/regexp.t starts `my ($file, $iters); BEGIN { $iters = shift || 1; $file = shift; ... }`.

MINIMAL REPRODUCER (probed perl 5.40.3 vs 209e7533 / s494u tree; scratch/s494u/ro6*.pl in the s494u worktree):
    ro6-inner.pl:   my ($file);
                    BEGIN { $file = 7; }
                    print "inner $file\n";
                    1;
    ro6.pl:         for $file ("./ro6-inner.pl") { do $file or die "do: $@"; }
  perl:  inner 7
  PCL:   do: Modification of a read-only value attempted at (eval 1) line 1.
  Without the BEGIN (`$file = 7;` at run time) PCL prints `inner 7`.  With `for my $f (...)` in the caller it works (nothing is aliased read-only).  Run DIRECTLY (not through do) the inner file is right, and a do'd file that assigns $main::file first shows lex/pkg distinct -- so the wrong target is specific to a BEGIN-time write of a file lexical in a do'd/required file.
LIKELY SHAPE (not verified): the BEGIN body is compiled/run before the file lexical's cell exists (or is resolved through the package in module mode), so the write lands on the package symbol `$file` of the current package -- the one the caller's foreach aliased; the read-only literal (s497b) only made the pre-existing wrong target LOUD.  Check whether the write went to $main::file before s497b too (silent wrong then).
BAR: ro6 = perl; the seven files back to at least their snapshot rows (regexp_normal.t 2021/8 ...); companion re/ leg A/B'd; sweep; gate.
